WEBVTT

00:00.480 --> 00:02.110
In the present time.

00:02.620 --> 00:05.900
With VR headgear,
you can go into a virtual world

00:05.900 --> 00:09.000
and play as the resident of that world.

00:09.570 --> 00:13.790
VR Full-Dive games are
at the height of their popularity.

00:14.900 --> 00:17.830
And there exists

00:17.830 --> 00:21.960
a god-tier game that stands
above all other games

00:21.960 --> 00:24.630
with over thirty million
players worldwide.

00:24.630 --> 00:26.380
And the name of that game is...

00:26.870 --> 00:29.100
Shangri-La Frontier.

00:50.200 --> 00:56.120
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

02:06.190 --> 02:10.860
#27: AN UNFRIENDLY GATE GUARD

02:12.570 --> 02:15.490
The forge should be down here.

02:16.530 --> 02:20.330
And maajiik ahhplikation yuunit
should also be there, right?

02:37.850 --> 02:40.140
It's pretty deep.

02:40.140 --> 02:43.640
Hmm, and I doubt there'd be
a cushion at the bottom.

02:43.640 --> 02:45.230
What now?

02:45.230 --> 02:46.650
I got a rope.

02:46.650 --> 02:48.280
Oh, that's great!

02:48.280 --> 02:49.270
In that case, let's...

02:53.530 --> 02:57.530
We gotta help each other
in times of need, don't we?

03:03.200 --> 03:04.540
Hold it!

03:09.540 --> 03:13.260
Since you ran, that means
you did see our messages.

03:13.260 --> 03:15.300
Sure is mean to ignore it, eh?

03:15.300 --> 03:17.350
If you have any last words, we'll listen.

03:17.840 --> 03:21.600
H-How did you guys find me?

03:21.600 --> 03:25.690
You shoved Crystal Scorpion
materials into Inventoria, didn't you?

03:27.060 --> 03:31.650
We'll have you talk about
how you got so much of it later.

03:32.400 --> 03:35.000
But that monster only spawns

03:35.000 --> 03:37.160
SPAWN = APPEAR
in the Crystal Cliff Nests, you know?

03:37.160 --> 03:39.490
Damn, I forgot!

03:39.490 --> 03:43.160
We all share the Inventoria!

03:43.160 --> 03:47.290
And knowing you, we figured
you already went on ahead,

03:47.290 --> 03:50.250
so we came here to Road of Past Glories.

03:51.170 --> 03:52.710
Damn it!

03:52.710 --> 03:55.590
Wh-Who are these gals?

03:55.590 --> 03:57.970
They are Mr. Sunraku's friends.

03:57.970 --> 04:02.470
That's right!
He's a valuable pawn... er, friend!

04:02.470 --> 04:04.640
You're tipping your hand.

04:05.180 --> 04:08.980
Also, I'm more curious
about this black rabbit and cat.

04:09.770 --> 04:12.940
How kind of you to ask!
I am Sword Master, known as the Wild Wi...

04:12.940 --> 04:15.230
We don't have time for that, okay?

04:15.860 --> 04:20.910
They're from the Unique Scenario you
can only dream of getting, OiKatzo.

04:20.910 --> 04:23.200
This is the blacksmith...

04:23.200 --> 04:24.450
I'm Bilac.

04:24.450 --> 04:25.700
And the Sword Master...

04:26.160 --> 04:28.120
I'm Aramis!

04:29.790 --> 04:32.170
You sure made quite the progress.

04:32.170 --> 04:34.210
U... U...

04:35.130 --> 04:39.630
Unique Scenario...?!

04:39.630 --> 04:42.140
His symptoms got worse, eh?

04:42.140 --> 04:46.430
Damn it! Why I'm the only
one who can't find one?!

04:46.430 --> 04:49.140
Well, not much you can do
when luck is involved.

04:49.640 --> 04:53.360
We can talk about
your messages later.

04:53.360 --> 04:56.530
Pawns or not, can you guys lend me a hand?

04:57.530 --> 05:00.570
About that Non-Standard Ether Reactor...

05:01.910 --> 05:04.990
To fulfill the requirement for fixing it,

05:04.990 --> 05:08.540
I need an item called
"Magic Application Unit."

05:10.540 --> 05:13.710
And it is likely somewhere
at the bottom of here.

05:14.920 --> 05:18.920
So, OiKatzo, would you mind
bungee jumping down for me?

05:18.920 --> 05:19.670
Huh?

05:20.080 --> 05:22.930
Why me? Why don't you do it yourself?

05:22.930 --> 05:26.560
I see! If that's the case, let's jump in!

05:26.560 --> 05:27.890
Katzo, you first.

05:27.890 --> 05:32.230
What? You instantly betrayed me?
What a monster.

05:33.560 --> 05:35.110
I mean, yeah, fine.

05:41.320 --> 05:44.570
I should be able to reach the bottom
by tying a few ropes together.

05:48.620 --> 05:52.370
Nobody got an idea what's down there,
but she sure got guts for going in anyway.

05:52.370 --> 05:55.290
If there is something,
I bet she'll just hop back up.

05:55.290 --> 05:57.630
You really think of her as your pawn, huh?

06:06.970 --> 06:10.470
It sure looks like those
sci-fi underground caverns.

06:11.520 --> 06:14.980
All good here! Doesn't seem
like there's any enemy around!

06:15.480 --> 06:18.410
Great.
How about we go in too?

06:23.990 --> 06:26.490
But man, what a surprise.

06:26.490 --> 06:31.870
It looks like a ruin outside,
but this joint is still running.

06:31.870 --> 06:34.420
Who would've thought
it'd be brighter down here.

06:37.840 --> 06:39.750
Huh? What's this?

06:40.710 --> 06:44.260
Uh, well, seems like
the security is still running, too.

06:52.270 --> 06:54.230
What's that thing?

06:54.230 --> 06:56.730
Kinda looks like Wethermon,
don't you think?

06:56.730 --> 06:57.770
What did you say?!

06:58.190 --> 06:59.480
Oh, c'mon.

06:59.480 --> 07:03.990
It better not be another "lock you
in combat for 30 minutes" thing again!

07:03.990 --> 07:07.990
But it does look like another
"high-mobility" type.

07:10.620 --> 07:13.790
But if we don't take that
thing down, that door...

07:13.790 --> 07:17.250
Yeah, beyond that
is likely the forge.

07:17.250 --> 07:20.170
And that guy seems like
the gate guard.

07:20.800 --> 07:24.390
Are we sure we're good here?

07:24.390 --> 07:27.760
Fret not, my black lass.

07:30.390 --> 07:35.560
No foe can match my blade!

07:36.230 --> 07:37.480
Sworvant's Solo...

07:37.900 --> 07:39.900
Primal Slash!

07:56.410 --> 07:59.710
Although it was an appreciable distance...

07:59.710 --> 08:01.460
...it managed to block my attack.

08:01.460 --> 08:05.090
That thing is clearly different
from the other golems.

08:05.090 --> 08:06.720
It's no big deal.

08:09.470 --> 08:12.930
We got the trio who beat a Colossus.

08:13.290 --> 08:17.940
This is the first time Wolf-Gang
has come together since its inception.

08:20.440 --> 08:22.690
CLAN "WOLF-GANG"

08:22.690 --> 08:25.780
We'll push our way through, four-arms!

08:25.780 --> 08:29.820
Vorpal Blade Arts:
Lakemirror Moon Version 3!

08:37.080 --> 08:39.210
Good job getting his attention!

08:39.210 --> 08:41.580
Use this chance to close in!

08:42.130 --> 08:44.630
Wall-running is an essential skill!

08:48.260 --> 08:49.550
It can shoot laser beams?!

08:51.050 --> 08:52.300
Gotcha!

08:52.300 --> 08:53.680
You're wide open!

08:57.930 --> 09:00.940
You got a nice shield!

09:03.900 --> 09:05.320
It's inside...

09:07.230 --> 09:08.190
Whoa!

09:09.360 --> 09:10.820
What a watchdog.

09:10.820 --> 09:13.700
Prioritizing guarding the gate
over the enemy, eh?

09:15.330 --> 09:16.410
But...!

09:20.370 --> 09:23.630
That's a bad choice, right?

09:31.260 --> 09:32.890
Sworvant's Solo...

09:32.890 --> 09:34.640
Add Spell!

09:35.140 --> 09:36.890
- Primal Slash!
- Magic Edge!

09:57.450 --> 09:58.700
Now...

10:00.830 --> 10:02.620
...for the barrage!

10:03.040 --> 10:05.330
All or Nothing!

10:08.840 --> 10:11.840
ALL OR NOTHING

10:16.760 --> 10:21.310
Usually, you'd be a decently tough foe...

10:21.310 --> 10:22.430
...but sorry.

10:23.230 --> 10:24.520
Our party...

10:25.440 --> 10:28.940
...only has attackers!

10:32.280 --> 10:34.820
Titan Blast!

10:34.820 --> 10:37.200
Dark Overstrike!

10:37.530 --> 10:40.080
Glowing Pierce!

10:54.070 --> 10:56.890
To think we'd win
by simply bulldozing through.

10:57.430 --> 11:01.140
A party of nothing but attackers
is usually a disadvantage.

11:01.140 --> 11:02.680
Mr. Sunraku!

11:03.180 --> 11:04.230
My beloved!

11:04.230 --> 11:06.280
Too easy! Too easy!

11:12.480 --> 11:14.990
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

11:16.030 --> 11:17.700
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

11:17.700 --> 11:18.990
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON
Yup, as I expected.

11:18.990 --> 11:19.620
Yup, as I expected.

11:19.620 --> 11:22.410
That didn't even put
a scratch in this.

11:22.410 --> 11:26.040
Is that the main weapon
you were lending out?

11:26.040 --> 11:27.540
Yeah.

11:27.540 --> 11:29.670
The Holy Spear Caled-fwlch.

11:29.670 --> 11:33.420
One of the only five Hero Weapons
that exist in this game.

11:33.870 --> 11:37.280
Owning one unlocks
the Hero Job for you.

11:37.280 --> 11:41.430
I went through a lot of trouble
to get my hands on this.

11:42.390 --> 11:45.940
If you're a Hero, SLF is doomed.

11:45.940 --> 11:51.270
Oh, don't be silly.
A hero is just a glorified assassin.

11:51.270 --> 11:53.360
Aah, there she said it.

11:54.360 --> 11:55.950
I blew it again.

11:58.450 --> 12:01.700
Still having trouble opening that door?

12:01.700 --> 12:05.500
You're the one who said you can
open it with your skill, you know?

12:05.500 --> 12:08.540
The skill's still at level 1, okay!

12:08.540 --> 12:10.500
It's got a low chance of success!

12:15.130 --> 12:16.530
Treasure Hunter skill.

12:17.130 --> 12:18.340
Ruins Sense.

12:18.340 --> 12:21.390
RUINS SENSE
ASSESS RUINS AND ANALYZE THEIR CONSTRUCTIONS

12:24.640 --> 12:26.310
Failed again.

12:26.310 --> 12:27.940
Can I go take a bath?

12:28.390 --> 12:32.860
I thought beating that four-arms would
get us a card key as a drop or something.

12:32.860 --> 12:34.900
But I guess it won't be that easy.

12:34.900 --> 12:37.280
It's time for the RNG challenge.

12:38.780 --> 12:40.660
RNG, huh...

12:40.660 --> 12:42.950
That never gives me good memories.

12:42.950 --> 12:47.330
They've never been
too kind to you, after all.

12:48.040 --> 12:50.370
All-Heart Chronicle, was it?

12:50.370 --> 12:52.710
ALL-HEART CHRONICLE
Where you need this one item

12:52.710 --> 12:54.420
ALL-HEART CHRONICLE
to heal the heroine's illness...

12:54.420 --> 12:56.050
ALL-HEART CHRONICLE
...but it took you three weeks

12:56.050 --> 12:57.720
ALL-HEART CHRONICLE
or retries to finally get it.

12:57.720 --> 12:59.510
Don't remind me of that!

13:00.430 --> 13:04.510
And that game turned into
All-Death Chronicle!

13:06.920 --> 13:10.600
Hey, Katzo! Hurry up and
get the lucky result already!

13:10.600 --> 13:13.730
I'm having my old trauma dragged up here!

13:22.740 --> 13:24.740
Analyze succeed!

13:24.740 --> 13:30.290
Looks like it's made to open when you
load in a working Legacy Weapon.

13:30.700 --> 13:34.000
Well, just shows the skill difference
between you and me, eh, Sunraku?

13:34.000 --> 13:37.450
Big talk for someone who can't even
trigger his own Unique Scenario.

13:42.890 --> 13:44.970
Whoa! Awesome!

13:44.970 --> 13:47.060
It's so spacious in here!

13:48.430 --> 13:50.640
Definitely what you'd call a laboratory.

13:50.640 --> 13:52.560
Yup, I can smell it!

13:52.560 --> 13:55.940
This place oozes rare items!

13:56.650 --> 14:00.470
All right, let's split up
and ransack this place, then.

14:01.490 --> 14:05.880
The Magic Application Unit
has to be here somewhere.

14:06.810 --> 14:08.410
He sure sounds really excited.

14:09.120 --> 14:11.460
I bet he just can't wait
to play with a new toy.

14:11.870 --> 14:13.960
I'll find it first!

14:15.960 --> 14:18.340
Looks kinda fun.

14:43.360 --> 14:45.740
A hologram?

14:45.740 --> 14:48.530
Quite a freaky-looking monster.

14:48.530 --> 14:49.910
Gross.

14:50.910 --> 14:54.370
Could this be one of the invaders
that people here fought?

14:57.330 --> 14:59.130
This mark looks familiar.

15:00.330 --> 15:01.960
Oh, right, it's the Omega symbol.

15:03.050 --> 15:07.970
You typically see them on some
secret weapon or boss monster.

15:09.850 --> 15:12.640
Still can't quite grasp
this world's setting yet.

15:14.350 --> 15:15.350
Hey.

15:15.350 --> 15:16.980
I know.

15:16.980 --> 15:18.440
What's the matter?

15:18.440 --> 15:20.730
No, nothing.

15:23.150 --> 15:26.530
But it sure seems like
a lot of work to find it here.

15:27.660 --> 15:29.620
It's a key item, right?

15:29.620 --> 15:31.740
It won't be easy to find.

15:32.110 --> 15:35.620
Besides, do we even know
what the thing looks like?

15:35.620 --> 15:36.870
Good question.

15:37.500 --> 15:41.840
Maajiik ahhplikation yuunit
is around this size.

15:42.320 --> 15:44.200
Mr. Sunraku! Mr. Sunraku!

15:45.880 --> 15:48.800
What do you think?
It's pretty cool, huh?

15:49.890 --> 15:52.470
What are you playing with?

15:52.470 --> 15:56.100
I found this stuck under
the desk over there.

15:56.640 --> 16:00.150
Anyway, just toss it away somewhere, okay?

16:02.570 --> 16:04.610
It's shaped like...

16:05.900 --> 16:07.570
Down we go.

16:10.320 --> 16:13.080
Th... That's it!

16:13.480 --> 16:14.710
Huh? What?

16:15.660 --> 16:18.120
That thingie Emul put on!

16:19.500 --> 16:25.010
Th-This is the maajiik ahhplikation yuunit
we're looking for!

16:25.010 --> 16:26.510
For real?!

16:26.510 --> 16:28.970
I found it!

16:28.970 --> 16:32.010
Oho! As expected from
my beloved's sister!

16:32.010 --> 16:36.140
With this, I can learn more
about Divinity-era weapons!

16:38.310 --> 16:40.520
Good job, Emul!

16:40.520 --> 16:43.360
Bilac! We've got no time to waste!

16:43.360 --> 16:46.030
Let's dash back to Rabitz
and get ready to...

16:48.650 --> 16:54.160
It's clear to us that you wanna take
the chance and run away, Sunraku.

16:54.160 --> 16:57.370
Don't tell us you forgot
about ignoring our messages.

17:05.880 --> 17:08.170
There are people
who want to meet me?

17:08.800 --> 17:13.890
Since our relationship got aired out
in public after we defeated Wethermon,

17:13.890 --> 17:16.640
we've had to deal with a lot of crap.

17:18.310 --> 17:24.440
I got surrounded by crazy-lookin' group
persistently pressing me about your rabbit,

17:24.440 --> 17:28.400
telling me to meet you up with them.
It was horrifying.

17:28.400 --> 17:29.320
Y'know that?

17:30.740 --> 17:32.240
As for me...

17:32.820 --> 17:36.830
The head of Schwarz Vulf
and Attack Master herself

17:36.830 --> 17:39.580
personally came up to negotiate with me.

17:39.580 --> 17:41.330
That's not my problem.

17:42.040 --> 17:45.340
Hm? Then that means...

17:45.340 --> 17:48.590
...you haven't met anyone
from Library yet?

17:49.090 --> 17:52.260
Huh? The Library?
You mean that lore clan?

17:52.260 --> 17:53.210
Crap!

17:54.220 --> 17:58.640
Sunraku! Did you
sell me off to that old man?!

17:58.640 --> 18:00.390
How could you!

18:00.390 --> 18:03.730
I can't deal with a guy like him.
He keeps badgering me with questions.

18:03.730 --> 18:07.320
Look, I'm just trying
to enjoy this game too, okay?

18:07.320 --> 18:08.900
Oh, come on...

18:12.150 --> 18:14.610
Wait, I can use this...

18:15.020 --> 18:20.660
Besides, I got this Magic Application Unit
event to work through, y'know?

18:20.660 --> 18:23.040
Do you need Sunraku for that?

18:23.040 --> 18:25.630
Nah, I can go ahead
and do the rest myself.

18:26.790 --> 18:28.380
You heard her.

18:28.380 --> 18:29.300
Figured.

18:29.300 --> 18:31.550
C'mon, help me out.

18:31.550 --> 18:33.800
Not my problem.

18:34.170 --> 18:38.180
Very different to how you would
treat me, right, my black lass?

18:38.180 --> 18:40.470
You ain't making any sense!

18:42.350 --> 18:46.900
How about we have the black bunny
have the Magic Application Unit

18:46.900 --> 18:49.210
and head back to Eighdold for now?

18:49.870 --> 18:51.940
We can discuss the details after that.

18:52.820 --> 18:55.280
No escaping this now, huh?

18:55.280 --> 18:56.660
Nuh-uh.

19:03.000 --> 19:04.660
Sunraku...

19:04.660 --> 19:06.290
Do you...

19:06.290 --> 19:09.210
...always dress like that when in town?

19:09.210 --> 19:11.380
What else can I do?

19:11.380 --> 19:14.720
This is the best way
to hide these guys.

19:15.470 --> 19:20.220
It's a headgear, so I can still equip it
even under the effect of Lycaon's Mark.

19:20.650 --> 19:23.730
Oh, I thought you walk around
half-naked because you like it.

19:23.730 --> 19:25.560
Hell no!

19:25.560 --> 19:27.980
I want to try out a lot of gear, too!

19:28.980 --> 19:34.240
Damn it, why must I play a game
that has this much freedom with a handicap?!

19:34.650 --> 19:37.300
Just get going already, okay!

19:37.300 --> 19:38.990
It's so cramped here, I can't take it!

19:38.990 --> 19:42.080
My beloved! There's plenty of space
within my embrace!

19:48.500 --> 19:53.260
Okay, I'll be taking this
maajiik ahhplikation yuunit.

19:53.260 --> 19:55.220
Yeah, it's all yours.

19:55.220 --> 19:58.010
I'm looking forward to seeing
"Bilac the Ancient Craftsman."

19:58.010 --> 19:59.800
Thanks for your help too, Aramis.

19:59.800 --> 20:03.680
I'll always swing by
and save my beloved from danger!

20:04.270 --> 20:06.100
We're leaving.

20:06.100 --> 20:08.190
Get moving, Moron-mis.

20:08.600 --> 20:09.570
Farewell!

20:15.360 --> 20:19.450
Honestly, I'd prefer it if you
could stay put in Rabitz, Emul.

20:19.450 --> 20:21.950
You wanna leave me behind again?

20:21.950 --> 20:25.620
I have no idea what they're
scheming for me, so...

20:25.620 --> 20:28.620
We've actually got a role
in mind for you, Emul.

20:28.620 --> 20:30.540
So we need you to stick around.

20:32.340 --> 20:33.750
Role?

20:47.180 --> 20:53.650
F... F... Found... you!

20:53.650 --> 20:56.150
Wh-What?!

20:59.070 --> 21:02.070
Emul!

21:05.950 --> 21:09.920
Emul!

22:43.760 --> 22:46.760
SLF Theater!

22:46.760 --> 22:47.600
#32 ANSWER IN 5 SECONDS OIKATZO

22:47.600 --> 22:49.100
#32 ANSWER IN 5 SECONDS OIKATZO
Mini!

22:49.100 --> 22:50.180
#32 ANSWER IN 5 SECONDS OIKATZO

22:53.440 --> 22:55.440
WHAT'S YOUR GAMEPLAY STYLE?

22:55.440 --> 22:58.190
Logical. All thorough.

22:59.570 --> 23:00.940
DO YOU KNOW THAT ACQUA PAZZA

23:00.940 --> 23:04.280
CONTAINS THE WORDS FOR "WATER" AND "CRAZY"?
Huh... So that's what it means?

23:04.950 --> 23:06.240
Wait, that's all?

23:07.070 --> 23:09.330
WHAT DO YOU THINK ABOUT SUNRAKU?

23:09.330 --> 23:14.330
The person I owe for— no, the root cause
of why I got into playing trash games.

23:14.580 --> 23:16.830
WHAT DO YOU THINK ABOUT PENCILGON?

23:16.830 --> 23:19.960
A pain to have as an enemy.
Even more of a pain as an ally.

23:19.960 --> 23:21.840
Her whole existence is a pain.

23:22.090 --> 23:23.840
DO YOU KNOW THE DIFFERENCE BETWEEN
BOUILLABAISSE AND ACQUA PAZZA?

23:23.840 --> 23:25.300
No, I don't.

23:26.510 --> 23:30.720
Um, why are you trying to make me
learn about western food?

23:30.970 --> 23:32.970
COULD YOU GIVE US SOME ROFL
ULTIMATE HILARIOUS MONK PUN?

23:32.970 --> 23:35.350
Huh? Hmm...

23:35.980 --> 23:39.510
"A-Are you sure you want to
mess with a Monk, ya punk?"

23:41.860 --> 23:42.730
5 POINTS

23:42.730 --> 23:44.740
5 POINTS
I'll freaking smack your butt, Sunraku...
